{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789253668,"nonce":"Siq+kFiM6uWAV7ZW/ZfSmxcHcWw=","title":"Python: async def, await and match","message":"`async def` is refused (the test for unsupported forms uses it). The\ncompiler has async natively, so `async def` maps to an async function,\n`await` to Await, and `asyncio.run`/`gather`/`sleep` to the executor\n(cc21fbc) once imports exist. Async generators and `async for`/`async\nwith` come after 4f32f29.\n\n`match` is a desugar onto TypedPattern, which already has Or, Guard,\nRest, At, Constructor and Map; class patterns need the class index\ntest, mapping patterns the dict primitives, and the subject is\nevaluated once into a temp.","files":null}]}